  "notes": "Transcribed from the official College of Marin Catalog 2018-2019 (marin.edu), 'NURSING EDUCATION: REGISTERED' program pages (pp. 203-205), 'Suggested Sequence of Courses'. Modeled as professional-phase per build.py convention: the catalog sequences only the four-semester professional phase taken after admission; the catalog states 'The curriculum is offered in four semesters' and 'it is strongly recommended that all prerequisites and corequisites for registered nursing licensure and the Associate of Science degree be taken prior to entry into the program.' Prerequisite sciences (BIOL 120 Human Anatomy, BIOL 224 Human Physiology, BIOL 240 Microbiology - each 4-5 units with lab; CHEM 110/114/115; ENGL 150; MATH 101 prerequisite / MATH 103 degree requirement) are carried under external_prereqs. NE 95 (Success in the Registered Nursing Program, 'to be taken once admitted to the Program') is a degree requirement with no published units in this catalog and no term in the suggested sequence; carried under external_prereqs. Remaining GE (American Institutions 3, Humanities 3, Physical Education 1, Cross Cultural Studies 3) carried under external_prereqs as ANY-MARIN-* slots. Semester sums 17.5 + 12.5 + 12.5 + 11.0 = 53.5; the catalog's TOTAL DEGREE UNITS 66.5 = 53.5 sequence + 13.0 additional GE, verified. The sequence lists 'Communication Skills Requirement 3' in BOTH Semester 1 and Semester 4; these are encoded as two distinct requirements per the catalog's own arithmetic (Speech degree requirement in Sem 1; GE Communication and Analytical Thinking in Sem 4). Advancement rule per catalog: 'Only those completing all the nursing requirements of a semester may advance to the following semester' - encoded as each semester's NE courses requiring the prior semester's NE courses. Students must earn 75+ in theory courses and Pass in clinicals. The newer Career Education catalog (cte.marin.edu, rev 03/24) confirms the same four-semester core progression and adds NE 95 to Fall 1 (units not stated there either).",
